---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | ctrl-cv" description="How ctrl-cv handles your account information and clips.">
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 8, 2026</p>

    <p>ctrl-cv is a clipboard for AI assistants, operated by ctrl-io ("we"). This policy explains what we collect, why, and the choices you have. Questions go to <a href="mailto:help@ctrl-cv.io">help@ctrl-cv.io</a>.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google account information.</strong> When you sign in with Google, we receive your Google account identifier and email address. We ask only for these.</li>
      <li><strong>Clips.</strong> The text you tell an AI to copy to ctrl-cv, along with its id, length, a short preview, and its order and expiry time.</li>
      <li><strong>Connection data.</strong> Sign-in sessions, and the tokens that let your AI apps reach your clipboard, including tokens issued by Google.</li>
      <li><strong>Service logs.</strong> Request details such as IP address, browser or app type, address requested, and time, plus clip ids, clip lengths, and a one-way hash of your account identifier. Clip text is not written to our logs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>ctrl-cv does not read your AI conversations. It receives only the text an AI sends when you ask it to copy.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>We use this information to sign you in, store and return your clips, keep the service secure, investigate problems, and respond to you. We don't sell your information, show ads, or use your clips to train AI models. We access clip content only when needed to operate the service, to investigate abuse or a problem you report, or when the law requires it.</p>
    <p>Our use of information received from Google APIs follows the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>

    <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Cloud</strong> hosts the service and stores clips and connection data, in the United States.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> provides sign-in.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides domain name service and forwards email sent to our help address.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts this website.</li>
      <li><strong>Your AI apps.</strong> When you ask an AI to paste a clip, its text goes to that AI's provider and is handled under that provider's terms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also disclose information when the law requires it. If you use ctrl-cv from outside the United States, your information is transferred to and processed there.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Clips</strong> are deleted automatically 30 days after they are saved. An expired clip stops being available immediately, and removal from storage can take a day or more. If you reach your account's storage limit, your oldest clips are removed first.</li>
      <li><strong>Your account record</strong> is deleted 30 days after your last copy, or when you delete all your clips.</li>
      <li><strong>Web sessions</strong> expire after 7 days. Expired sign-in and connection records can't be used, and may stay in storage in encrypted form until they are cleaned up.</li>
      <li><strong>Service logs</strong> are kept for about 30 days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>Data is encrypted in transit and at rest. Tokens and session data are additionally encrypted by the application. Each clip is tied to one account and can't be read from another. No service is perfectly secure, so please don't save passwords, keys, or other secrets as clips.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>View and delete your clips, one at a time or all at once, at <a href="https://ctrl-cv.io/clips">ctrl-cv.io/clips</a>.</li>
      <li>Disconnect ctrl-cv in your AI app, or remove its access from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account</a>.</li>
      <li>Contact <a href="mailto:help@ctrl-cv.io">help@ctrl-cv.io</a> to ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of your information. You may have further rights where you live.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>ctrl-cv is not for anyone under 14, or under the minimum age for using online services without parental consent where they live. If you believe a child has used it, contact us and we will delete the information.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. When we do, we will change the date above, and for significant changes we will give notice through the service.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
